@baseUrl = http://localhost:4004/invoice-review

### Create Data (deep insert: email -> invoices -> lineItems)
# NOTE: property names are case-sensitive and must match the CDS model:
#   - key element is `ID` (uppercase, from `cuid`), not `id`
#   - `verificationStatus` is an association -> set the FK `verificationStatus_code`
#   - there is no `summary` field on Emails
# The service is NON-DRAFT, so this POST creates the record directly (no
# IsActiveEntity, no draftActivate). Under --profile s4 the create is bridged
# to S/4's draft flow by the s4-proxy write handlers.
POST {{baseUrl}}/Emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "ID": "e1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
    "emailSubject": "Test",
    "emailSentDate": "2026-07-23T13:09:10+08:00",
    "emailSender": "aismail@abeam.com",
    "emailBodyHtml": "test",
    "summary": "test",
    "invoices": [
        {
            "ID": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
            "documentNumber": "25016078",
            "documentDate": "2025-12-10",
            "totalAmount": 292680.00,
            "currency": "MYR",
            "taxAmount": 21680.00,
            "vendorCode": "100234",
            "vendorName": "Zaid Ibrahim & Co",
            "vendorAccountNumber": "21433400001867",
            "verificationStatus_code": "P",
            "lineItems": [
                {
                    "ID": "aaaa1111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
                    "amount": 292680.00,
                    "glAccount": "6100100",
                    "costCenter": "108-02600",
                    "internalOrder": "PTR121-115"
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}

### Read back the email with its invoices + line items
GET {{baseUrl}}/Emails(e1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111)?$expand=invoices($expand=lineItems)
